<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chikka Vira Rajendra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chikka Vira Rajendra was the last raja of Coorg (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kodagu">Kodagu</a>), in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reigning from 1820 to 1834. Accused of misrule and hostility to the British, he was deposed by an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> force in 1834, and Coorg was annexed. He lived in exile, travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, where his daughter was baptised with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> as godmother, and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chikka-vira-rajendra.jpg" alt="Chikka Vira Rajendra" width="204" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Chikka_Veera_Rajah,_the_last_King_of_Coorg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
